        <li><a href="#third-party">Third-Party Services</a></li>
        <li><a href="#cookies">Cookies and Analytics</a></li>
        <li><a href="#marketing">Marketing Communications</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sharing">Sharing Information</a></li>
        <li><a href="#security">Data Security</a></li>
        <li><a href="#retention">Data Retention</a></li>
        <li><a href="#choices">Your Choices</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes to This Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Contact Us</a></li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <section id="information-we-collect">
      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect information including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Parent or guardian name</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Phone number</li>
        <li>Billing and transaction information</li>
        <li>Athlete name, age, grade, and sport</li>
        <li>Program registrations and participation history</li>
        <li>Membership information</li>
        <li>Communications and inquiries</li>
        <li>Information you voluntarily provide through forms</li>
        <li>Website usage and device information, such as browser type, IP address, cookies, and analytics data</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Payment information may be processed directly by third-party payment providers. The Courts may not directly store complete payment card information.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="how-we-use-information">
      <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
      <p>We may use information to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Manage memberships, registrations, and purchases</li>
        <li>Communicate with families about schedules, programs, events, and facility updates</li>
        <li>Provide customer and member support</li>
        <li>Match athletes with appropriate programs or coaches</li>
        <li>Process payments and transactions</li>
        <li>Improve our programs, website, and member experience</li>
        <li>Send news and marketing communications where permitted</li>
        <li>Maintain safety and facility operations</li>
        <li>Prevent fraud or misuse</li>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="children">
      <h2>Information About Athletes and Children</h2>
      <p>The Courts serves youth athletes, but our website, registration, purchasing, and account features are intended to be used by parents, guardians, and other adults, not independently by children under 13.</p>
      <p>Parents and guardians may provide information about their children when registering for programs or communicating with The Courts.</p>
      <p>Children under 13 should not independently submit personal information through our website.</p>
      <p>If we learn that personal information has been collected directly online from a child under 13 in a manner requiring parental consent, we will take appropriate steps consistent with applicable law.</p>
      <p>Parents or guardians who believe a child has submitted personal information directly to us may contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@playthecourts.com">hello@playthecourts.com</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="third-party">
      <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>We may use third-party providers to support our operations, including services for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Membership and program registration</li>
        <li>Scheduling</li>
        <li>Payment processing</li>
        <li>Website hosting</li>
        <li>E-commerce and merchandise</li>
        <li>Email communications</li>
        <li>Analytics</li>
        <li>Forms and customer communications</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These providers may process information as necessary to provide their services.</p>
      <div class="legal-note" style="background:#FDE7F0; border-left-color:#E0369D; color:#8A1F63;">Note for final version: specifically identify Upper Hand, Fourthwall, our payment processor, analytics provider, email platform, and any other material services once the final tech stack is confirmed.</div>
    </section>

    <section id="cookies">
      <h2>Cookies and Analytics</h2>
      <p>Our website may use cookies and similar technologies to operate the site, understand how visitors use it, improve performance, and support marketing.</p>
      <p>You may be able to control certain cookies through your browser or available cookie-management tools.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="marketing">
      <h2>Marketing Communications</h2>
      <p>If you sign up to receive updates from The Courts, we may send you information about programs, camps, clinics, leagues, events, merchandise, and other Courts news.</p>
      <p>You may unsubscribe from marketing emails at any time using the unsubscribe link included in those messages.</p>
      <p>You may still receive operational communications related to memberships, purchases, registrations, schedules, safety, or other transactions.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="sharing">
      <h2>Sharing Information</h2>
      <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>
      <p>We may share information with service providers that help us operate The Courts, process transactions, deliver programs, maintain our website, or communicate with families.</p>
      <p>We may also disclose information where required by law, necessary to protect safety or legal rights, or as part of a business transaction involving The Courts.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="security">
      <h2>Data Security</h2>
      <p>We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational measures designed to protect personal information.</p>
      <p>No online system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="retention">
      <h2>Data Retention</h2>
      <p>We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes for which it was collected, our legitimate business needs, and applicable legal, accounting, or reporting requirements.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="choices">
      <h2>Your Choices</h2>
      <p>You may contact us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Update or correct information</li>
        <li>Request information about data we maintain</li>
        <li>Ask us to delete information where appropriate</li>
        <li>Change your communication preferences</li>
        <li>Ask a privacy-related question</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Certain information may need to be retained for legal, safety, accounting, or operational purposes.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. Updates will be posted on this page with a revised &ldquo;Last Updated&rdquo; date.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy?</p>
      <p>The Courts, LLC<br>2011 Johnson Industrial Blvd.<br>Nolensville, TN 37086<br><a href="mailto:hello@playthecourts.com">hello@playthecourts.com</a></p>
    </section>
